  "body": "The definitions of \"Continue\" and \"Break\" in the [Iteration](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#algorithm-iteration) section should be clear on what the definitions mean in nested loops.  Given that the behavior in most programming languages is that they apply to the inner-most loop, I suspect this is the behavior that's desired.  However, I think it should be stated explicitly.\r\n\r\nIn other words, I think it should be stated explicitly somewhere that something like:\r\n\r\n1. For each doc in docs:\r\n   1. ...\r\n   2. While true:\r\n       1. ...\r\n       2. If X, Continue\r\n\r\nThe \"Continue\" continues to the next iteration of \"While true\", not to the next iteration of \"For each doc in docs\".",
